@* "Install the ACA360 app" popup, shown by js/pwa.js on the first page after signing in, only when
   this browser can install ACA360 and it is not installed yet. "Not now" (or closing it) asks again
   after 14 days on this device; "Don't ask again" stops it (the profile menu item stays).
   iPhone / iPad have no install button, so the steps are shown instead. *@
<div class="modal fade" id="installAppModal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="installAppTitle" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header border-0 pb-0">
                <h5 class="modal-title" id="installAppTitle">Install the ACA360 app</h5>
                <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body">
                <div class="d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                    <img src="~/icons/icon-192.png" alt="" width="56" height="56" class="rounded-3 flex-shrink-0" />
                    <div>
                        <p class="mb-2">Open ACA360 straight from your desktop, Start menu or home screen, in its own window like any other app.</p>
                        <p class="mb-0 small text-muted" data-install-steps="ios">
                            On iPhone or iPad: tap <strong>Share</strong> <i class="bx bx-share"></i>, then <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-footer border-0 pt-0">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-link text-muted me-auto px-0" data-install-choice="never">Don't ask again</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-label-secondary" data-install-choice="later">Not now</button>
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" data-install-choice="install"><i class="bx bx-download me-1"></i> Install</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
